# A call to a tool the request did not offer stays text, as before and as TensorFold's server since 7be90a36b and
# 806af974c (v1.0.0 on, callName returns an offered name or nothing), and is now reported (#103). The call is never
# made and never run; a one-call reply drops it as before. parse_tool_calls takes a `rejected` list and gets the name
# of each block that parsed as a call (GLM, Qwen or JSON markup) to an unoffered tool (prose that only names the tags
# is no block: 0112). The server logs one line for such a reply,
# `[tensorfold] tool call rejected: unknown_tool_name ['exec'] (2 tools offered); kept as text` (names only, never an
# argument); TF_GLM_TOOL_DIAGNOSTICS=1 also lists them in the reply's `tensorfold` block (a stream's last event) as
# `tool_call_rejections: [{"reason": "unknown_tool_name", "name": "exec"}]`, so a gateway can tell the reply from an
# ordinary answer and re-prompt. Tokens, content, calls and finish_reason are unchanged. Adapted from BadAd84's
# patch 0114 (#137). CPU check: tools/test_unoffered_tool_call.py.
diff --git tensorfold/cuda/reply_text.py tensorfold/cuda/reply_text.py
--- tensorfold/cuda/reply_text.py
